  "notes": [
    "This document is the Stratum-3+ (+/-0.1 ppm, order code 'Q'), plain TCXO (pin 1 = OE), 10 MHz LVCMOS, 3.3 V, Extended-Industrial (-40 to +105 C) grade. The +/-0.2 ppm and +/-0.25 ppm (Stratum 3, codes 'P'/'N') grades, the VCTCXO (voltage-controlled) and DCTCXO (I2C digital-pull) configurations, and the -20 to +70 / -40 to +85 temperature options are separate orderable grades with different specs (per the one-grade-per-document rule) and are not folded in here.",
    "SiTime prints stability, tolerance, sensitivity, hysteresis, aging and the temperature slope in ppb (and ppb/C). All are normalized to ppm (and ppm/C) at 1 ppb = 1e-3 ppm; the original ppb figures are preserved in each conditionsVerbatim.",
    "Because this is the +/-0.1 ppm grade, the +/-4.6 ppm 20-Year Total Stability (F_tot_20y) figure is NOT applicable - it is printed only for the Stratum 3 (+/-0.2/+/-0.25 ppm) grade table and would belong to those separate grade documents. This grade's aging and holdover carry its long-term budget instead.",
    "Guaranteed specs printed with no dictionary key, kept only here: Mechanical Shock Resistance 30000 g (MIL-STD-883F Method 2002) and Mechanical Vibration Resistance 70 g (Method 2007) - mechanical survival ratings distinct from the ppb/g fractional-frequency g_sensitivity; Maximum Operating Junction Temperature table (Table 10) mapping ambient to Tj (e.g. 105 C ambient -> 115 C Tj), a derating guide rather than a single value.",
    "Spurious for this -40 to +105 C grade at 3.3 V is -112/-106 dBc; the -40 to +85 C jitter/phase-noise table (Table 4) instead prints -112/-105 dBc, and Table 6 also lists -112/-101 dBc at Vdd = 2.5 V.",
    "Idd/I_od supply currents are specified by the datasheet at F_nom = 19.2 MHz (not at this part's 10 MHz output); the 19.2 MHz reference condition is retained on those measurements."
  ],
